  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the calculation of the aspiration level (2250€), the differences between outcomes and this level, and the probability of positive differences — is not mentioned in the verbal report. The individual does not reference the mean of outcomes or deviations from it. Instead, the justification is based solely on the probability of winning (90% vs. 45%) and the perceived security of the outcome, without reference to positive differences or aspiration levels. While the individual does consider the probability of positive outcomes (winning money), they do so in a qualitative, intuitive way (‘very high probability’), not by comparing the probability of positive deviations from a mean. Therefore, the decision reason — which requires explicit consideration of the aspiration level and the probability of positive differences from it — is not used. The individual’s reasoning is qualitatively similar in outcome (prefers A), but the underlying mechanism is different. There is no evidence of applying the decision reason’s rule. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
